WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.333
Build a small image set from the actual use case.

00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:08.143
Include ordinary examples, difficult examples, and costly edge cases.

00:00:08.143 --> 00:00:12.376
For CCTV review, vary lighting, distance, occlusion, and harmless activity.

00:00:12.376 --> 00:00:16.186
For OCR, vary font size, layout, blur, and contrast.

00:00:16.186 --> 00:00:20.419
Create expected answers or a scoring rubric before comparing models.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:25.076
Score factual visual grounding, task completion, unsupported claims, format, and usefulness.

00:00:25.076 --> 00:00:30.155
Keep human scoring consistent and preserve examples that expose important failure modes.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:31.849
Run each configuration repeatedly.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:36.082
Measure accuracy, completion rate, latency, throughput, memory, power where relevant,

00:00:36.082 --> 00:00:36.929
and consistency.

00:00:36.929 --> 00:00:43.702
Separate cold-start time from steady inference and record failures or empty outputs rather than excluding them.

00:00:43.702 --> 00:00:44.548
Control variables.

00:00:44.548 --> 00:00:48.781
Record model and vision-adapter versions, quantization, runner, backend, prompt template,

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.591
image settings, context, thinking mode, generation parameters, and hardware.

00:00:52.591 --> 00:00:56.401
A result without configuration detail cannot guide deployment reliably.

00:00:56.401 --> 00:01:01.904
Use generic public benchmarks as background, not as a substitute for local evidence.

00:01:01.904 --> 00:01:06.561
The 23-model, 30-image, three-run benchmark illustrates tiered selection and repeat testing,

00:01:06.561 --> 00:01:10.371
but rankings will age as models and runtimes change.

00:01:10.371 --> 00:01:15.027
Maintain an evaluation log with dates, results, decisions, and rejected alternatives.

00:01:15.027 --> 00:01:20.107
Re-run the suite after model, quantization, runtime, driver, prompt, or hardware changes.

00:01:20.107 --> 00:01:24.340
The benchmark is a living acceptance test for the workflow.
